{"product_id":"practical-php-and-mysql","title":"Practical PHP and MySQL","description":"\"Practical PHP and MySQL reflects Jono's commitment to the spirit of making open source subjects accessible to everyone. The book carefully walks you through the code for eight useful, dynamic Web applications. Projects are presented in a playful way, like the forum project that touts horror movies that make you 'hide behind the couch.'\" -From the Foreword by Christopher Negus, Series Editor, Negus Live Linux Series Build Dynamic Web Sites Fast, with PHP and MySQL... Learn from Eight Ready-to-Run Applications! nbsp; Suddenly, itrsquo;seasyto build commercial-quality Web applications using free and open source software. With this book, yoursquo;ll learn from eight ready-to-run, real-world applicationsâall backed by clear diagrams and screenshots, well-documented code, and simple, practical explanations. nbsp; Leading open source author Jono Bacon teaches the core skills yoursquo;ll need to build virtually any application. Yoursquo;ll discover how to connect with databases, upload content, perform cascading deletes, edit records, validate registrations, specify user security, create reusable components, use PEAR extensions, and even build Ajax applications. nbsp; Working from complete examples on the CD-ROM, yoursquo;ll create Generic dynamic Web sites Blogs Discussion forums Shopping carts Auction sites Calendars FAQ systems Reusable components Content management systems News sites nbsp; JONO BACONis Ubuntu community manager for Canonical, Ubuntursquo;s sponsor. He is an established speaker, author, and contributor to the open source community. Bacon co-authoredLinux Desktop HacksandThe Official Ubuntu Book; has served as a columnist forLinux Format,Linux User \u0026amp; Developer, andPC Plus; and is an Orsquo;Reilly Networkweblog author. He is a lead developer onthe Jokosher (www.jokosher.org) project,and co-founder of LUGRadio-a podcastwith more than 15,000 listeners, andan annual event that attracts visitorsfrom around the world. nbsp; CD-ROM Includes XAMPP for Linux: easy-to-install, preconfigured Apache distributions containing MySQL, PHP, Perl, and more Source code for all eight fully-working applications discussed in the book A remastered Ubuntu live CD, set to run all eight applications live nbsp; System Requirements CPU: Pentium III, 650 MHz. RAM: 256MB (recommended 512MB). Hard disk: No space required to run live CD; 250MB of space needed to put XAMPP server and projects on installed system. \n Dimensions:176 x 232  \n Author: Jono Bacon \n ISBN: 9780132239974 \n Format: Paperback \n Pages 528","brand":"bookloopbook.com","offers":[{"title":"Default Title","offer_id":44268627132569,"sku":"3EDU9780132239974","price":40.0,"currency_code":"$","in_stock":true}],"thumbnail_url":"\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0580\/5696\/6297\/files\/bc074dfea719453cd518683a59fb82ab.jpg?v=1714555723","url":"https:\/\/bookloopbook.com\/products\/practical-php-and-mysql","provider":"Dubai - Buy Used\/Second-Hand Books - Book Loop Book","version":"1.0","type":"link"}